infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Queue vs topic: who gets the message?
  desc Same broker, two delivery models — one consumer claims the work, or every subscriber gets a copy
  compares
    - label Queue
      children
        - label Delivered to exactly one consumer
          desc Each message is claimed by a single worker, then deleted on ack
        - label Work is divided, not duplicated
          desc Add consumers to share load — each does part of the total
        - label Use it to distribute a job
          desc "Someone send this email" — only one worker should send it
    - label Topic
      children
        - label Delivered to all subscribers
          desc Every subscriber receives its own copy of the message
        - label Work is broadcast, not split
          desc Add subscribers to react in parallel — each gets the full stream
        - label Use it to fan out an event
          desc "User signed up" — billing, analytics, and email all react
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
